   At threads>1 a repeat analysis is not an independent replicate: it re-uses the same
   permutations, so re-running does not average the Monte-Carlo error away.

D. spread of the reported p-values over 20 repeats run as SEPARATE processes
   configuration              median sd    effective n      nominal iterations
   threads=1                  0.01275      1068             1000
   threads=4                  0.02764      270              1000

   'effective n' is p(1-p)/var(p_hat): the number of independent permutations that
   would produce the observed spread. At threads=4 it is about a quarter of the 1000
   iterations the user asked for, which is what 250 distinct permutations buys.
